Diagnosis

Relevant log lines: build command (line 53-line 55), tsc error causing failure (line 56) and the TypeScript JSX error (line 57).
Error type and cause: TypeScript error TS17008 — "JSX element 'div' has no corresponding closing tag." The TypeScript compiler points to components/ui/Layout.tsx at (137,10) as the location of the unbalanced JSX tag: https://github.com/HalagelIT/HALAGEL-MANUFACTURING-SYSTEM/blob/main/components/ui/Layout.tsx#L137.
Solution

Open the file components/ui/Layout.tsx at the referenced location: https://github.com/HalagelIT/HALAGEL-MANUFACTURING-SYSTEM/blob/main/components/ui/Layout.tsx#L137

Fix the unclosed/mismatched JSX tag. Locate the opening <div> around that line and add the matching closing </div> (or make it self-closing if that was intended). Example fix (illustrative) — ensure your JSX structure is balanced, e.g.:

// before (example problematic snippet)
return (
  <div className="layout">
    <header>...</header>
    <main>...</main>
  // missing closing tag here
);
// after (fixed)
return (
  <div className="layout">
    <header>...</header>
    <main>...</main>
  </div>
);
Verify locally:
Run TypeScript compilation to reproduce the error locally:
npm run build
or just tsc (if installed): npx tsc
Make sure linter/formatter (ESLint/Prettier) runs to catch these issues early.
Commit and push the fix, then re-trigger the Netlify build.
Notes / tips

The compiler reports the exact file/column — inspect nearby JSX blocks for other mismatches (nested tags or fragments).
If you use an editor/IDE with JSX/TSX support it will highlight unbalanced tags immediately.

